    },
    "lactation": {
      "level": "ok",
      "text": {
        "fa": "برچسب: مواجهه شیرخوار انتظار نمی‌رود.",
        "en": "Label: infant exposure not expected."
      },
      "quote": "Topical benzyl alcohol is unlikely to be absorbed through the skin of breastfeeding women in clinically relevant amounts; therefore, breastfeeding is not expected to result in exposure of the infant to NATROBA [ see Clinical Pharmacology (12.3) ].",
      "refs": [
        {
          "source": "fda-natroba",
          "section": "8.2"
        }
      ]
    },
    "pediatric": {
      "level": "caution",
      "text": {
        "fa": "برچسب برای کودکان شرط، محدودیت سنی یا نکته دارد؛ جمله برچسب در زیر آمده است.",
        "en": "The label has conditions, age limits or notes for children; the label sentence is quoted below."
      },
      "quote": "Head Lice Infestation The safety and effectiveness of NATROBA for the topical treatment of head lice infestation have been established in pediatric patients 6 months of age and older [see Clinical Pharmacology (12.3) and Clinical Studies (14) ] .",
      "refs": [
        {
          "source": "fda-natroba",
          "section": "8.4"
        }
